                                        <line x1="25" y1="5" x2="25" y2="20" stroke="#212529" stroke-width="2.5"/>
                                        <polygon points="12,20 38,20 25,36" fill="none" stroke="#212529" stroke-width="2.5"/>
                                    </svg>
                                    <div class="small text-muted">Signal Ground</div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                        <td>Acts as the common reference point (0 V) from which all other voltages in the circuit are measured.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </SubSection>

    <SubSection title="Using Circuits for Filtering" id="Filtering">
        <p>
            Due to the ways that circuit components affect voltage and current, circuits are a useful way for us to physically interact with signals without needing digital filtering or circuit analysis. We can construct circuits based on the parameters we need, which are current, voltage, and resistance.
        </p>
        <p>
            We can use this to construct physical filters. These allow us to avoid digital components and filters as they are often used to replicate the effect of physical components computationally. Using simple circuit components can reduce the footprint and the size scale of the device for portability and reduces energy consumption.
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive my-3">
            <table class="table table-bordered table-hover align-middle shadow-sm">
                <thead class="table-primary text-center">
                    <tr>
                        <th style="width: 45%;">Filter</th>
                        <th style="width: 55%;">Circuit</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="p-3">
                            <strong class="text-primary fs-6">Low Pass Filter:</strong> an RC filter circuit made out of a resistor (<InlineEquation equation="R"/>) and a capacitor (<InlineEquation equation="C"/>) connected together to reject all unwanted high frequency signals.
                            <div class="mt-2 text-muted small">
                                <strong>Cutoff Frequency:</strong> <InlineEquation equation="f_c = \\frac{1}{2\\pi RC}"/>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                        <td class="text-center p-3 bg-white">
                            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 150" class="img-fluid" style="max-width: 400px; width: 100%; height: auto;">
                                <circle cx="40" cy="75" r="20" fill="none" stroke="#0d6efd" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <path d="M 28 75 Q 34 65 40 75 T 52 75" fill="none" stroke="#0d6efd" stroke-width="1.8"/>
                                <text x="40" y="112" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0d6efd">Vin</text>
                                <line x1="40" y1="55" x2="40" y2="35" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <line x1="40" y1="35" x2="110" y2="35" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <path d="M 110 35 L 120 25 L 132 45 L 144 25 L 156 45 L 168 25 L 176 35" fill="none" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <text x="143" y="18" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#d97706">Resistor, R</text>
                                <line x1="176" y1="35" x2="250" y2="35" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <circle cx="250" cy="35" r="3" fill="#334155"/>
                                <line x1="250" y1="35" x2="340" y2="35" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <circle cx="340" cy="35" r="3.5" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#198754" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <!-- Capacitor C -->
                                <line x1="250" y1="35" x2="250" y2="68" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <line x1="230" y1="68" x2="270" y2="68" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="3"/>
                                <line x1="230" y1="78" x2="270" y2="78" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="3"/>
                                <rect x="230" y="69" width="40" height="8" fill="#0284c7" opacity="0.3"/>
                                <text x="185" y="77" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0284c7">Capacitor, C</text>
                                <line x1="250" y1="78" x2="250" y2="115" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <!-- Bottom -->
                                <line x1="40" y1="95" x2="40" y2="115" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <line x1="40" y1="115" x2="340" y2="115" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <circle cx="250" cy="115" r="3" fill="#334155"/>
                                <circle cx="340" cy="115" r="3.5" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#198754" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <!-- Ground -->
                                <line x1="250" y1="115" x2="250" y2="128" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <line x1="240" y1="128" x2="260" y2="128" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <line x1="243" y1="133" x2="257" y2="133" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                                <line x1="247" y1="138" x2="253" y2="138" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1"/>
                                <text x="360" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#198754">Vout</text>
                            </svg>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="p-3">
                            <strong class="text-primary fs-6">High Pass Filter:</strong> an RC filter circuit made out of a resistor (<InlineEquation equation="R"/>) and a capacitor (<InlineEquation equation="C"/>) connected together to modify, reshape or reject all unwanted low frequency signals to produce a first-order frequency response.
                            <div class="mt-2 text-muted small">
                                <strong>Cutoff Frequency:</strong> <InlineEquation equation="f_c = \\frac{1}{2\\pi RC}"/>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                        <td class="text-center p-3 bg-white">
                            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 150" class="img-fluid" style="max-width: 400px; width: 100%; height: auto;">
                                <circle cx="40" cy="75" r="20" fill="none" stroke="#0d6efd" stroke-width="2"/>
                                <path d="M 28 75 Q 34 65 40 75 T 52 75" fill="none" stroke="#0d6efd" stroke-width="1.8"/>
